caption: Universal engine
engine-rule: universal-engine

Psi Talented is Personally Instanced by default. The Tradition defines the legal scope of Power Talents available through it. That scope may be a closed list, a named published source-bounded catalog, or explicit construction rules. When a character gains access, they normally select two different legal Power Talents as the initial contents of their personal instance. A Tradition may require particular selections, restrict pairings, or explicitly use a different starting count.

Each selected Psi Power Talent costs 5 character points per level unless a more specific published or Tradition rule says otherwise. Both selected Talents begin with Advanced access. The practitioner may purchase legal abilities assigned to those Talents without separate ability-by-ability instruction unless the Domain or Tradition explicitly requires it.

Each ability is assigned to one governing Talent. A second Talent does not add to rolls or caps merely because it could also describe the ability. A Tradition may create an explicit interaction procedure, such as Revelator's Conjunction Powers.

The contents of a personal instance cannot be replaced through ordinary advancement, instruction, or Tradition Mastery unless the Tradition explicitly permits it. An explicit Tier 3 Tradition, Greater Wish, reality alteration, mutation, psychic reconstruction, or comparable extraordinary effect may alter a personal instance, but the effect must define how former Talent levels, previously purchased abilities, refunds, suppression, and future purchase permissions are handled.

A Tradition may explicitly expand the same personal instance as a unique benefit. Gifted Mind's third Talent at Mastery is the reference example; it enlarges that practitioner's personal instance rather than creating a second instance or invoking Talent Upgrade.

The character may buy only Power Talents contained in the personal instance and abilities assigned to those Talents, plus Basic or secondary access granted by Domain rules.

All traits use the required Psionic modifier and limitations.

The Tradition states the starting access band for every available Talent.

Tradition Mastery grants Master access to the initial selected Talents and their associated abilities. A Talent added by a Tradition-specific Mastery benefit uses the access band stated by that benefit; absent a stated exception, it also gains Master access.
